%% AI-agent event flow — maintenance request example
%% Sanitized: no real data, no operational internals (intervals, thresholds, or endpoint detail).
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant T as Tenant
    participant App as edpmanagement app
    participant FS as Firestore
    participant CF as Cloud Function (Firestore trigger)
    participant Q as Agent notification pipeline
    participant Sched as Scheduled escalation
    participant P as Pierce (AI property-management agent)
    participant H as Human (property mgr / owner)

    T->>App: Submit maintenance request
    App->>FS: Create maintenance record
    FS-->>CF: Trigger fires
    CF->>H: Notify human stakeholders (email / push)
    CF->>Q: Route a notification into the agent pipeline
    Note over CF,Q: Decoupled — the trigger completes regardless of agent availability

    P->>Q: Consume from the pipeline
    P->>App: Act within the property-management workflow
    Note over P,App: Agent actions are recorded to audit logs

    Sched->>H: Escalate requests that go stale
    Note over Sched,H: Responsibility is partitioned between escalation paths<br/>to prevent duplicate action

    Note over T,H: Ongoing work: capability-scoped authorization,<br/>server-side policy enforcement, and human-approval controls
